# T-1038: --- uses: ["core"] injects builtin-* aliases into document scope.
# Without it, builtin-* aliases are undefined and produce T002 warnings.
# This test confirms the baseline: WITH --- uses: ["core"], no T002 warning fires.
#
# Document isolation means the uses directive applies to THIS document only.
# Other documents in the same file (or files that include this one) do NOT
# automatically gain access to the injected builtin-* aliases.
#
# See raw_builtin_t002.llt-eval for the complementary test WITHOUT --- uses: ["core"].
--- uses: ["core"]
[result: [builtin-pow 2 10]]

=== out
Dict({"result": Float(1024)})
